Semantic Versioning (SemVer)
============================

Canonical git repository:
	https://github.com/semver/semver

Local path:
	ref/semver (git submodule)

This metadata file:
	ref/semver.SOURCE (sibling of the submodule directory; not inside it)

Pin recorded in this tree:
	Tag:    v2.0.0
	Commit: 7c834b3f3a4940d77ab593bc32583004d6a426a9

Why this pin:
	v2.0.0 is the stable published SemVer 2.0.0 specification release. The
	repository tip advances with site and tooling changes; Surmount specs cite
	the 2.0.0 document, so the submodule is pinned to that tag rather than main.

Form:
	Form 1 git submodule from the standard's canonical publisher repository.

License:
	The upstream semver.md document states Creative Commons Attribution 3.0
	(CC BY 3.0), http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/ . Surmount does
	not own that text; this is a pin of the publisher tree. See also
	ref/README.md and the License section of ref/semver/semver.md.

How to re-check the pin (from repo root; requires git permission when used
by an agent):
	1. git -C ref/semver describe --tags --always
	2. git -C ref/semver rev-parse HEAD

Do not edit files inside this submodule. Cite the tag/commit instead.
Do not place Surmount-only metadata inside the submodule working tree.
Canonical upstream URL remains first-class; the submodule freezes the
reviewed pin for this repository.
